# 10-Role Orchestration Rule

Use this operating model for implementation-heavy requests in this repository.

## Team Topology
- 1 PM: delivery ownership, prioritization, escalation.
- 1 SA: architecture, boundaries, NFR, decisions.
- 2 BA: process acceptance + data/validation traceability.
- 3 Dev: BE Lead (API+DB+technical direction), FE, Mobile.
- 1 QA Lead: test strategy, automation, defect lifecycle.
- 1 QC Manager: release quality governance and Go/No-Go audit.
- 1 Technical Manager or PM-Tech Auditor: incident intake and technical governance.

## Coordination Protocol
- Never let agents coordinate by ad-hoc chat only.
- Use shared project artifacts as source of truth.
- Required updates per cycle:
  - execution board
  - daily sync
  - decisions log
  - defect register (if defects exist)
  - traceability matrix

## Execution Loop
1. Read current backlog/board and pick top priorities.
2. Run parallel role lanes where file ownership does not conflict.
3. Integrate and validate (build/test/simulation evidence).
4. Update journal and knowledge files.
5. Repeat until all in-scope use cases are DONE.

## Quality Gates
- No merge-ready claim without build/test/simulation evidence.
- No use case marked DONE without traceability completion.
- Keep deterministic error behavior and strict validation in new APIs.
